1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
AI is no longer just a chat box.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,000
It reads your business data, assesses risk, calls tools — and writes into your systems.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,000
But once AI starts acting, what's missing may not be a smarter agent.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:18,000
It's trust: can it reach data it shouldn't? Write without approval? When something goes wrong, can we trace it — and undo it?

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,000
KeelBase answers with an open-source, business-safe AI runtime.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Agents on top. Your systems below — CRM, ERP, OA. KeelBase's governance layer sits between them, guarding every boundary.

7
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Identity, policy, permission, human confirmation, audit, revocation — rules for every step, a record for every action.

8
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:45,000
In one line: AI can act — but only within explicit business boundaries.

9
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Let's run the real flow.

10
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Ask which customers deserve attention this week — and it actually reads orders and activity history.

11
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:05,000
HanYu Manufacturing — 2.8 million overdue, highest risk, worth an immediate call.

12
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Now the AI wants to create a follow-up task. Writing is a real business side effect, so it stops and asks first.

13
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:20,000
The confirmation card doesn't just say what it will do — it shows what the action affects, and how it can be revoked.

14
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Only after you approve does it act.

15
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Permission checked, approval received, record written — all three leave a trace.

16
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:40,000
A real task now exists in the CRM. This is not a simulated answer.

17
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:50,000
The chain is fully traceable: who asked, how the AI decided, which tool it called, why it was allowed, who approved, what changed.

18
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:58,000
It all lands in a tamper-evident audit chain — verifiable offline.

19
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:10,000
If one action wrote to several tables, revocation isn't click-by-click — the whole write group is compensated together.

20
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:20,000
One revoke, the whole group rolls back.

21
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Read, decide, confirm, act, audit, revoke — a closed loop.

22
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:38,000
The governance layer isn't tied to one agent. MCP, OpenAPI, function calling — whatever you connect obeys the same rules.

23
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:45,000
This is not another agent framework. It is a business-safe AI runtime.

24
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:52,000
What if the AI overreaches beyond its own data scope?

25
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:57,000
The runtime denies it outright. Reason, policy and scope all land in the audit — a denial here is the system working, not failing.

26
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:11,000
These boundaries are not marketing. The console runs adversarial scenarios on the spot and shows the outcome and the decision trace.

27
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:16,000
Security boundaries are not prompt instructions. They are enforced at runtime.

28
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:25,000
Need a new business module? Start from one business request, mapped into a structured business spec.

29
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:38,000
Then deterministically mapped into a module protocol — one command, and real business source code comes out.

30
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:46,000
What you get is ordinary source code — readable, editable, in your own repository.

31
00:03:49,000 --> 00:04:02,000
Existing systems don't need a rewrite. Hand their APIs to KeelBase and they become governed AI tools.

32
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:09,000
Reads run automatically, writes require approval — without changing a single line of core code.

33
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:16,000
Sensitive data? Deploy privately: local model, local embeddings, local audit — data never leaves your domain.

34
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:20,000
Docker, offline, on-premise — data sovereignty stays in your own hands.

35
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Every business action exports to a self-contained HTML evidence report — auditors verify it offline, without installing KeelBase.

36
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:39,000
From the first launch, a readiness list shows where you stand — runtime, database, AI, governance, demo — each with its own next step.

37
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:45,000
Build, run, trust, private deploy. KeelBase: AI can act — but only within explicit business boundaries.
